After much trial and error, it seems the biggest contribution to slowing down my models is the addition of markocc = 0 to my capthist object. As I mentioned I have this set to all 0 to denote no specific 'marking' occasions. On reflection maybe this should be all 1s - any occasion can be a marking occasion because there can be a new cat to 'mark' (ie identify for the first time) on any day. That does fit much faster, <10 seconds for a null model, but is that the right approach? It also sometimes fails to produce SE estimates.

I suppose my general question here now is - what are marking and sighting/resighting in the context of camera traps where animals have never been physically trapped and marked?

