> > > > > > Hi Murray, thanks very much for the response
> > > > > >
> > > > > > Sorry, I may have got my terms mixed up - it's sighting-only in as much as there is no physical marking (ie from trapping/tagging), but we're using the individual pelage of cats to ID. So I suppose technically the first sighting of an identifiable individual is the 'marking'? Do I need to reflect that in the data somehow? At the moment I have set markocc in read.capthist set to all 0s. There are also unknown/unidentifiable cats in the data which I've included using addSightings() on the ID'd animals. I'm assuming that it's not known how many identifiable animals there are - perhaps I should switch that and assume that we HAVE captured every one?
> > > > > >
> > > > > > Looks like sigma/2 will actually produce a finer grid than I'm currently using but that's a handy guideline I'll keep in mind moving forward.
