Hi Murray
Hope you don't mind me chipping in here, I am supervising Roxy's research. I'm not sure what is going on but if I use the exact code that she posted along with the same parameter values that you used (D = 0.01 and lam0 = 0.1) I am still getting that error that refers to "missing value in parameter". I have also updated both secr and secrdesign to the latest versions. If I execute run.scenarios with fit = F it runs fine and I can see that the data summary looks fine i.e. there are plenty of individuals and recaptures. It seems that something is failing when trying to fit a model.

Here is the exact code FYI:

> D_val = 0.01 ; sig_val = 2000 ; lam0_val = 0.1

> reg_grid = make.grid(nx = 5, ny = 8, spacing = (2 * sig_val), detector = 'count', originxy = c(9000, 9000))
> alltrps = make.grid(nx = 36, ny = 36, spacing = (2/3)*sig_val,

